version: 2.0.0
components:
  help-view:
    description: In-app help system with 9-section guide covering Conductor capabilities, menus, shortcuts, and known limitations. Accessible via ? button.
    file: packages/conductor/Sources/Conductor/UI/Views/HelpView.swift
    type: view
  agent-decision:
    description: "Model for a host-rendered branching CHOICE the agent offers the human ($decision-exchange), parsed from a conductor-decision fenced block (#fenced-block-parser). Carries question + 2-5 DecisionOptions (label/description/★recommended/▸visualId) + multiSelect/allowOther + an optional settled DecisionAnswer. composeReply() builds the human-readable user turn. Lives on ConversationMessage (additive)."
    file: packages/conductor/Sources/Conductor/Models/AgentDecision.swift
    type: model
  agent-visual:
    description: "Model for a host-rendered DIAGRAM, COMPARISON or GRAPH ($decision-exchange), parsed from a conductor-visual envelope or a bare mermaid/svg fence (#fenced-block-parser). kind flow|comparison|graph render in v1 (LIGHTBOX); graph carries a GraphPayload (root/nodes/edges/truncated/freshness) drawn by #atrium-graph-view; wireframe|diff are decode-tolerant v2 placeholders. Rendered as a ▸ launcher chip — never auto-opens."
    file: packages/conductor/Sources/Conductor/Models/AgentVisual.swift
    type: model
  atrium-decision-card:
    description: "Inline card rendering an #agent-decision in the ATRIUM thread. PENDING = question + stacked radio/checkbox option cards + Other… field (when allowOther) + escape affordances, AMBER leading rail (Mika's temperature law); on pick calls onAnswer → ClaudeStreamSession.answerDecision. ANSWERED = collapsed teal ✓ you chose <label> with a change/reopen affordance. ★ marks a recommended lean; ▸ view opens a linked visual in the LIGHTBOX."
    file: packages/conductor/Sources/Conductor/UI/Views/Atrium/AtriumDecisionCard.swift
    type: view
  atrium-visual-canvas:
    description: "THE LIGHTBOX — a 380pt right slide-out hosting one #agent-visual. Shares the right zone with the CHORUS rail and renders OVER it (chorus stays mounted; PUSH-consistent layout, conversation column narrows). Switches on kind: flow → MermaidWebView (sandboxed offline WKWebView, vendored mermaid.min.js, NO network, ATRIUM-recolored); comparison → native SwiftUI table (ATRIUM styling); graph → #atrium-graph-view (❖ header glyph); wireframe/diff → v2 placeholder."
    file: packages/conductor/Sources/Conductor/UI/Views/Atrium/AtriumVisualCanvas.swift
    type: view
  atrium-graph-view:
    description: "Native SwiftUI Canvas render of a bounded symbol ego-graph (#agent-visual kind == .graph) inside THE LIGHTBOX. STATIC closed-form RING layout: root (focus) at center with a soft halo, other nodes evenly on a ring (angle 2π·i/count, radius shrunk to fit 380pt). Edges draw under nodes as center→ring lines. Node shapes encode GraphSymbolKind via Mika's accent mapping (component→ink rounded rect, flow→user stadium, gate→amber diamond, signal→teal circle, aspect→violet dashed). Labels = symbol id, scaled off atriumFontScale. Footer shows +N-more (truncated) + stale-index. NO force sim, drag, zoom, or hover in this cut."
    file: packages/conductor/Sources/Conductor/UI/Views/Atrium/AtriumGraphView.swift
    type: view
  mermaid-web-view:
    description: "Sandboxed WKWebView that renders a mermaid diagram OFFLINE from a vendored mermaid.min.js (Resources/, loaded via #conductor-resources to dodge the SwiftTerm Bundle.module collision). nil baseURL, navigation blocked except the in-memory load, ATRIUM dark theme. Degrades to a source dump if the script is missing from the bundle."
    file: packages/conductor/Sources/Conductor/UI/Views/Atrium/MermaidWebView.swift
    type: view
